From 324f0821362fabd3120e34e2f748f858b88b0e93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:01:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Stadium transformations: production byte-identical with
 them off and on frozen Stadium

Checked with game data, this series changed production output on every Pokemon Stadium game of the 92,
frozen ones included (lock frozenps: anim lines 9798 -> 7932). What ran with the setting off:

- Upstream fcc46464 (match termination timing, completed games frozen, save format v2) is not part of the
  stadium series any more: it stops stepping once the match is decided and moves the outcome check, for
  every stage, whatever the setting, so it cannot stay byte-identical. It is dropped, not gated.
- preload_match_configuration preloaded Pokemon Stadium with transformations forced on, so the frozen
  domain's GameData preload was a transforming match's. The frozen preloads now run exactly as before (no
  patch bits), and one transforming Stadium preload follows them all, before GameData seals.
- ft_80089B08's IK restore (msl_fighter_pose_srt_restored) changed the pose schedule of every fighter on
  every stage; it now applies only in a match with transformations on.
- Replay-derived configs (validate_replay, prepare_replay_benchmark) ask one helper,
  admission.stadium_transformations: Pokemon Stadium only, never when the capture says frozen
  (is_frozen_ps or the legacy FreezeStadium patch).

Defaults, all off: MslMatchConfig.stadium_transformations 0, melee_sim MatchConfig False, the live viewer's
stadiumTransformations false, the C config's slippi_patches bit 1 clear. Data-free test:
tests/test_stadium_transformation_gating.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
